1. **Let each inverse trigonometric expression be an angle and write its trigonometric ratio**
$\alpha=\arcsin\frac{8}{17}$
$\sin\alpha=\frac{8}{17}$
2. **Identify each angle's quadrant from the range of its inverse function**
$-\frac{\pi}{2}\le\alpha\le\frac{\pi}{2}$ and $\sin\alpha>0$, so $\alpha$ is in quadrant 1.
3. **Use a right-angled triangle and Pythagoras to find the remaining ratios with the correct signs**
$\text{adjacent}=\sqrt{17^{2}-8^{2}}$
$=15$
$\cos\alpha=\frac{15}{17}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.7]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.55,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0,1.36);
\draw (C) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$15$};
\draw (B) -- (A) node[midway, above right] {$17$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, left] {$8$};
\coordinate (c1) at ($(C)!0.2cm!(B)$);
\coordinate (c2) at ($(C)!0.2cm!(A)$);
\draw (c1) -- ($(c1)+(c2)-(C)$) -- (c2);
\pic[draw,"$\alpha$",angle radius=0.5cm,angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle=A--B--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
4. **Substitute into the double angle or compound angle identity**
$\sin 2\alpha=2\sin\alpha\cos\alpha$
$=2\times\frac{8}{17}\times\frac{15}{17}$
$=\frac{240}{289}$

